IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 1, RULE 3: THE GENERAL DEFINITIONS, one function per defined term.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Every function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the thing is within the term as the Rules define it.
--   JUST FALSE   the Rules say, in the words of the definition, that it is not.
--   NOTHING      the definition does not answer: it says "includes" and the list is not closed,
--                or it points to a provision, an Act or a power outside the sources, or its own
--                wording limits the grant ("where appropriate", "in cases where ... empowered").
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- "UNLESS THE CONTEXT OTHERWISE REQUIRES".  Rule 3(1) opens with these words, so every
-- definition below can be displaced by context.  The first function takes that as a plain input;
-- no other function threads it, because a judgment about context is the reader's, not a fact.
--
-- THE BORROWED FACTS.  A definition that "has the meaning given by" another provision, or that
-- points to a Schedule, is asked as an input NAMED FOR THE PROVISION ANSWERING IT, with the type
-- `MAYBE BOOLEAN`: JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE when that provision has answered, NOTHING when not.
-- Those provisions are in other parts' ranges, so they are seams (PLAN.md).



-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 1, Rules 1 and 2 -- commencement, application and transitional provisions`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- the day the Rules come into operation`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:11 | 1. These Rules are the Rules of Court 2021 and come into operation on 1 April 2022.
@ref O 1 r 1 (src:11)
`o 1 r 1 the day these Rules come into operation` MEANS Date 1 4 2022

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- the facts the paragraphs ask about`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- What kind of proceedings, as paragraphs (3) to (12) sort them.  The court and the date come from
-- the core's `Action`: for an appeal or an originating application to an appellate court, the date
-- is the date it was filed.
DECLARE `o 1 r 2 kind of proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `o 1 r 2(3)(a) civil proceedings in the Supreme Court or the State Courts`
    `o 1 r 2(8) proceedings under the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    `o 1 r 2(10)(b) proceedings in the General Division transferred out to the Singapore International Commercial Court`
    `o 1 r 2(10)(c) proceedings for the transfer of a case from the General Division to the Singapore International Commercial Court`
    `o 1 r 2(10)(d) an appeal or an originating application to the Court of Appeal relating to a decision of the Singapore International Commercial Court`
    `o 1 r 2(11) item 1 proceedings under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `o 1 r 2(11) item 2 proceedings relating to the winding up of limited liability partnerships`
    `o 1 r 2(11) item 3 proceedings relating to the winding up or receivership of variable capital companies or their sub-funds`
    `o 1 r 2(11) item 4 proceedings under Part IV of the Parliamentary Elections Act`
    `o 1 r 2 other proceedings`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2(2) and (6) -- the First Schedule saves the revoked Rules`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:13 | 2. —(1) Subject to the following provisions of this Rule, the Rules of Court (R 5) (called the revoked Rules of Court) are revoked. (2) The saving and transitional provisions set out in the First Schedule have effect.
@ref O 1 r 2(1) and (2) (src:13)
GIVEN `the provision is set out in the First Schedule as a saving or transitional provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(2) a saving or transitional provision has effect` MEANS
    IF `the provision is set out in the First Schedule as a saving or transitional provision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The saving and transitional provisions set out in the First Schedule have effect"

-- src:49 | (6) Where the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division hears an appeal under these Rules against a decision of a lower Court which was made in proceedings governed by the revoked Rules of Court, these Rules do not apply to any proceedings in the lower Court following the appeal before the Court of Appeal or Appellate Division, and the revoked Rules of Court continue to apply to any such proceedings in the lower Court following the appeal in accordance with the First Schedule.
@ref O 1 r 2(6) (src:49)
GIVEN `the decision appealed against was made in proceedings governed by the revoked Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division hears the appeal under these Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(6) these Rules apply to the proceedings in the lower Court following the appeal` MEANS
    IF `the decision appealed against was made in proceedings governed by the revoked Rules of Court` AND `the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division hears the appeal under these Rules`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "these Rules do not apply to any proceedings in the lower Court following the appeal"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (6) speaks only of an appeal from proceedings governed by the revoked Rules

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2(3) -- the Rules apply to proceedings commenced on or after 1 April 2022`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:14 | (3) Subject to this Rule, these Rules — ( a )
-- src:15 | apply to and in relation to all civil proceedings in the Supreme Court or the State Courts which are commenced on or after 1 April 2022, including appeals arising from those proceedings; and
@ref O 1 r 2(3)(a) (src:14-15)
GIVEN action IS AN Action
      kind IS A `o 1 r 2 kind of proceedings`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(3)(a) these Rules apply to civil proceedings commenced on or after 1 April 2022` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(3)(a) civil proceedings in the Supreme Court or the State Courts` AND action's `action commenced on` AT LEAST `o 1 r 1 the day these Rules come into operation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which are commenced on or after 1 April 2022"

-- src:16 | ( b )
-- src:17 | apply with the necessary modifications to and in relation to every appeal to the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division, and every originating application to the Court of Appeal or Appellate Division, which is filed on or after 1 April 2022, relating to a decision of a lower Court made in proceedings to which the revoked Rules of Court apply (whether under the First Schedule or otherwise).
@ref O 1 r 2(3)(b) (src:16-17)
GIVEN action IS AN Action
      `the decision is of a lower Court and was made in proceedings to which the revoked Rules of Court apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(3)(b) these Rules apply with modifications to an appeal or originating application to an appellate court` MEANS
    IF    (   action's `action court level` EQUALS `Court of Appeal`
           OR action's `action court level` EQUALS `Appellate Division`)
      AND action's `action commenced on` AT LEAST `o 1 r 1 the day these Rules come into operation`
      AND `the decision is of a lower Court and was made in proceedings to which the revoked Rules of Court apply`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which is filed on or after 1 April 2022, relating to a decision of a lower Court made in proceedings to which the revoked Rules of Court apply"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2(4) -- notices of appeal and applications for permission against decisions made before 1 April 2022`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Each function below finds WHERE the period starts, or WHICH period applies.  Whether a filing was
-- in time is a comparison with the last day that O 3 r 3 counts: the input
-- `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`.  The text fixes a period for each in its own words, so a
-- filing outside the period answers JUST FALSE (ruling (a) of 2026-11-05: a period the text fixes in
-- its own words gives JUST FALSE outside it); O 3 r 4 lets the Court extend it, and that is O 3 r 4's.

DECLARE `o 1 r 2(4)(a) how the decision came to be made` IS ONE OF
    `o 1 r 2(4)(a)(i) an order made in chambers`
    `o 1 r 2(4)(a)(ii) the refusal of an application`
    `o 1 r 2(4)(a)(iii) a case in which a request for further arguments was made under section 29B(2) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act`
    `o 1 r 2(4)(a)(iv) any other case`

-- src:18 | (4) For the purposes of paragraph (3)( b ) — ( a )
-- src:19 | subject to sub‑paragraph ( b ), the notice of appeal against a judgment or order of the General Division or Appellate Division given or made before 1 April 2022 must be filed and served within one month after — (i)
-- src:20 | in the case of an appeal from an order made in chambers — the date when the order was pronounced or when the appellant first had notice of the order;
-- src:21 | (ii)
-- src:22 | in the case of an appeal against the refusal of an application — the date of the refusal;
-- src:23 | (iii)
-- src:24 | in a case where a request for further arguments was made under section 29B(2) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act — the date mentioned in section 29B(4)( b ) of that Act; or
-- src:25 | (iv)
-- src:26 | in any other case — the date on which the judgment or order appealed against was pronounced;
@ref O 1 r 2(4)(a) (src:18-26)
GIVEN how IS A `o 1 r 2(4)(a) how the decision came to be made`
      `the date the order was pronounced` IS A DATE
      `the date the appellant first had notice of the order` IS A DATE
      `the date of the refusal` IS A DATE
      `section 29B(4)(b) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act the date mentioned` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the judgment or order appealed against was pronounced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 1 r 2(4)(a) the date after which the one month for the notice of appeal runs` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `o 1 r 2(4)(a)(i) an order made in chambers` THEN
        IF `the date the order was pronounced` EQUALS `the date the appellant first had notice of the order`
        THEN JUST `the date the order was pronounced`
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "the date when the order was pronounced or when the appellant first had notice of the order" does not say which of two different dates counts
    WHEN `o 1 r 2(4)(a)(ii) the refusal of an application` THEN JUST `the date of the refusal`
    WHEN `o 1 r 2(4)(a)(iii) a case in which a request for further arguments was made under section 29B(2) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act` THEN `section 29B(4)(b) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act the date mentioned` -- NOTHING-kind when absent (points outside the text): section 29B(4)(b) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act
    WHEN `o 1 r 2(4)(a)(iv) any other case` THEN JUST `the date the judgment or order appealed against was pronounced`

-- src:18 | (4) For the purposes of paragraph (3)( b ) — ( a )
-- src:19 | subject to sub‑paragraph ( b ), the notice of appeal against a judgment or order of the General Division or Appellate Division given or made before 1 April 2022 must be filed and served within one month after — (i)
@ref O 1 r 2(4)(a) the period (src:18-19)
`o 1 r 2(4)(a) one month` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 1
    `period unit` IS Months
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

@ref O 1 r 2(4)(a) (src:18-19)
GIVEN `the date the notice of appeal is filed` IS A DATE
      `the date the notice of appeal is served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(4)(a) the notice of appeal is filed and served within one month` MEANS
    IF `the date the notice of appeal is filed` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` AND `the date the notice of appeal is served` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text fixes the period in its own words): "must be filed and served within one month after"

-- src:27 | ( b )
-- src:28 | where permission to appeal against a decision of the General Division or Appellate Division is required, the notice of appeal against the decision of the General Division or Appellate Division made before 1 April 2022 must be filed and served — (i)
-- src:29 | where the application for permission to appeal is filed before that date — within one month after the date on which such permission is granted; or
-- src:30 | (ii)
-- src:31 | where the application for permission to appeal is filed on or after that date — within 14 days after the date on which such permission is granted; and
@ref O 1 r 2(4)(b) (src:27-31)
GIVEN `the application for permission to appeal was filed on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A Period
`o 1 r 2(4)(b) the period after permission is granted` MEANS
    IF `the application for permission to appeal was filed on` LESS THAN `o 1 r 1 the day these Rules come into operation`
    THEN Period WITH
        `period length` IS 1
        `period unit` IS Months
        `period direction` IS `After the anchor`
    ELSE Period WITH
        `period length` IS 14
        `period unit` IS Days
        `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

@ref O 1 r 2(4)(b) (src:27-31)
GIVEN `the date the notice of appeal is filed` IS A DATE
      `the date the notice of appeal is served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(4)(b) the notice of appeal is filed and served within the period after permission` MEANS
    IF `the date the notice of appeal is filed` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` AND `the date the notice of appeal is served` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text fixes the period in its own words): "within one month after the date on which such permission is granted" or "within 14 days after the date on which such permission is granted"

DECLARE `o 1 r 2(4)(c) how the time for the permission application begins` IS ONE OF
    `o 1 r 2(4)(c)(i) section 29B does not apply`
    `o 1 r 2(4)(c)(ii)(A) the Judge heard further arguments and affirmed, varied or set aside the decision`
    `o 1 r 2(4)(c)(ii)(B) a request for further arguments was made and the Judge certified, or is deemed to have certified, that none are required`
    `o 1 r 2(4)(c)(ii)(C) section 29B applies in any other case`

-- src:32 | ( c )
-- src:33 | an application for permission to appeal against a decision of the General Division or Appellate Division made before 1 April 2022 must be filed and served, together with the documents mentioned in Order 18, Rule 29(7) or Order 19, Rule 26(7) (as the case may be) — (i)
-- src:34 | within 7 working days after the date of the decision of the lower Court; or
-- src:35 | (ii)
-- src:36 | where section 29B of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act applies, within 7 working days after — (A)
-- src:37 | in a case where the Judge who made the decision hears further arguments in respect of the decision — the date the Judge affirms, varies or sets aside the decision after hearing further arguments;
-- src:38 | (B)
-- src:39 | in a case where a request for further arguments was made, but the Judge who made the decision certifies, or is deemed to have certified, that no further arguments are required — the date the Judge certifies, or is deemed to have certified, that no further arguments are required; or
-- src:40 | (C)
-- src:41 | in any other case — the earlier of the following: (CA)
-- src:42 | the time at which the judgment or order relating to the decision is extracted;
-- src:43 | (CB)
-- src:44 | the 15th day after the date on which the decision is made.
@ref O 1 r 2(4)(c) (src:32-44)
GIVEN how IS A `o 1 r 2(4)(c) how the time for the permission application begins`
      `the date of the decision of the lower Court` IS A DATE
      `the date the Judge affirmed, varied or set aside the decision after further arguments` IS A DATE
      `the date the Judge certified, or is deemed to have certified, that no further arguments are required` IS A DATE
      `the time the judgment or order was extracted` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`o 1 r 2(4)(c) the date after which the 7 working days for the permission application run` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `o 1 r 2(4)(c)(i) section 29B does not apply` THEN `the date of the decision of the lower Court`
    WHEN `o 1 r 2(4)(c)(ii)(A) the Judge heard further arguments and affirmed, varied or set aside the decision` THEN `the date the Judge affirmed, varied or set aside the decision after further arguments`
    WHEN `o 1 r 2(4)(c)(ii)(B) a request for further arguments was made and the Judge certified, or is deemed to have certified, that none are required` THEN `the date the Judge certified, or is deemed to have certified, that no further arguments are required`
    WHEN `o 1 r 2(4)(c)(ii)(C) section 29B applies in any other case` THEN
        CONSIDER `the time the judgment or order was extracted`
        WHEN JUST extracted THEN `the earlier of` extracted (`the date of the decision of the lower Court` PLUS 15)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date of the decision of the lower Court` PLUS 15

-- src:33 | an application for permission to appeal against a decision of the General Division or Appellate Division made before 1 April 2022 must be filed and served, together with the documents mentioned in Order 18, Rule 29(7) or Order 19, Rule 26(7) (as the case may be) — (i)
-- src:34 | within 7 working days after the date of the decision of the lower Court; or
@ref O 1 r 2(4)(c) the period (src:33-34)
`o 1 r 2(4)(c) seven working days` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 7
    `period unit` IS `Working days`
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

@ref O 1 r 2(4)(c) (src:33-34)
GIVEN `the date the application for permission is filed` IS A DATE
      `the date the application for permission is served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `o 18 r 29(7) or o 19 r 26(7) the documents mentioned are filed and served with it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(4)(c) the application for permission to appeal is filed and served in time with its documents` MEANS
    IF `the date the application for permission is filed` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` AND `the date the application for permission is served` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `o 18 r 29(7) or o 19 r 26(7) the documents mentioned are filed and served with it`
        WHEN JUST documents THEN
            IF documents
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "together with the documents mentioned in Order 18, Rule 29(7) or Order 19, Rule 26(7) (as the case may be)"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Order 18, Rule 29(7) and Order 19, Rule 26(7) are in other parts' ranges
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text fixes the period in its own words): "within 7 working days after"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2(5) -- the modified rules on permission to appeal`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:45 | (5) Order 18, Rule 29 and Order 19, Rule 26 (as the case may be) apply to and in relation to an application for permission to appeal mentioned in paragraph (4)( c ) subject to the following modifications: ( a )
-- src:46 | Order 18, Rule 29(1) to (4) and Order 19, Rule 26(1) to (4) do not apply;
@ref O 1 r 2(5)(a) (src:45-46)
GIVEN `order number` IS A STRING
      `rule number` IS A STRING
      `paragraph number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(5)(a) a paragraph applies to an application for permission mentioned in paragraph (4)(c)` MEANS
    IF (   (`order number` EQUALS "18" AND `rule number` EQUALS "29")
        OR (`order number` EQUALS "19" AND `rule number` EQUALS "26"))
       AND `paragraph number` AT LEAST 1 AND `paragraph number` AT MOST 4
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Order 18, Rule 29(1) to (4) and Order 19, Rule 26(1) to (4) do not apply"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (5)(a) disapplies only paragraphs (1) to (4) of those two Rules

DECLARE `o 1 r 2(5)(b) the time provided under the Rule` IS ONE OF
    `o 1 r 2(5)(b) the time in paragraph (4)(c)(i)`
    `o 1 r 2(5)(b) the time in paragraph (4)(c)(ii)`

-- src:47 | ( b )
-- src:48 | the references to “the time provided under this Rule” in Order 18, Rule 29(6)( a ) and Order 19, Rule 26(6)( a ) are to be read as references to the time provided under paragraph (4)( c )(i) or (ii).
@ref O 1 r 2(5)(b) (src:47-48)
GIVEN `section 29B of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `o 1 r 2(5)(b) the time provided under the Rule`
`o 1 r 2(5)(b) the time provided under the Rule is the time in paragraph (4)(c)(i) or (ii)` MEANS
    IF `section 29B of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act applies`
    THEN `o 1 r 2(5)(b) the time in paragraph (4)(c)(ii)`
    ELSE `o 1 r 2(5)(b) the time in paragraph (4)(c)(i)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2(7) -- the Court may direct that provisions apply despite the revoked Rules`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:50 | (7) Despite any provision in these Rules providing that the revoked Rules of Court are to apply to certain proceedings, the Court may direct that the provisions of Order 3, Rule 8, Order 8, Rule 2 or 4A, Order 25, Rule 3(2), Order 29A, Order 55 or Order 64, Rule 4 or 4A are to apply with suitable modifications to those proceedings. [S 293/2022 wef 03/04/2022]
@ref O 1 r 2(7) (src:50)
GIVEN `order number` IS A STRING
      `rule number` IS A STRING
      `the revoked Rules of Court apply to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(7) the Court may direct that a provision applies with suitable modifications` MEANS
    -- "Order 29A" and "Order 55" are cited whole: every rule of those Orders matches, whatever `rule number` is.
    IF `the revoked Rules of Court apply to the proceedings` AND (
           (`order number` EQUALS "3" AND `rule number` EQUALS "8")
        OR (`order number` EQUALS "8" AND `rule number` EQUALS "2")
        OR (`order number` EQUALS "8" AND `rule number` EQUALS "4A")
        OR (`order number` EQUALS "25" AND `rule number` EQUALS "3(2)")
        OR (`order number` EQUALS "29A")
        OR (`order number` EQUALS "55")
        OR (`order number` EQUALS "64" AND `rule number` EQUALS "4")
        OR (`order number` EQUALS "64" AND `rule number` EQUALS "4A"))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is given for the listed provisions of Order 3, Order 8, Order 25, Order 29A, Order 55 and Order 64 only

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2(8) to (13) -- proceedings to which the Rules do not apply`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:52 | (8) These Rules do not apply to proceedings under the Criminal Procedure Code 2010, unless otherwise provided in the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 or any subsidiary legislation made thereunder. [S 758/2025 wef 31/12/2025]
@ref O 1 r 2(8) (src:52)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 1 r 2 kind of proceedings`
      `the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 or its subsidiary legislation provides otherwise` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(8) these Rules apply to proceedings under the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(8) proceedings under the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    THEN
        CONSIDER `the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 or its subsidiary legislation provides otherwise`
        WHEN JUST otherwise THEN
            IF otherwise
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 says how these Rules apply
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "These Rules do not apply to proceedings under the Criminal Procedure Code 2010"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 provides otherwise is not among the sources
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (8) speaks only of proceedings under the Criminal Procedure Code 2010

-- src:53 | (9) These Rules do not apply to proceedings in the Family Division of the High Court.
@ref O 1 r 2(9) (src:53)
GIVEN action IS AN Action
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(9) these Rules apply to proceedings in the Family Division of the High Court` MEANS
    IF action's `action court level` EQUALS `Family Division`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "These Rules do not apply to proceedings in the Family Division of the High Court"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (9) speaks only of proceedings in the Family Division

-- src:54 | (10) Unless the Court otherwise directs, and subject to any other written law, these Rules do not apply to — ( a )
-- src:55 | any proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court commenced on or after 1 April 2022;
-- src:56 | ( b )
-- src:57 | any proceedings commenced on or after 1 April 2022 in the General Division that are transferred out to the Singapore International Commercial Court;
-- src:58 | ( c )
-- src:59 | any proceedings (whether upon application or on the General Division’s own motion) for the transfer of a case from the General Division to the Singapore International Commercial Court, where the case is commenced on or after 1 April 2022; or
-- src:60 | ( d )
-- src:61 | any appeal to the Court of Appeal, or any originating application to the Court of Appeal, filed on or after 1 April 2022, relating to a decision of the Singapore International Commercial Court.
@ref O 1 r 2(10) the four kinds of proceedings (src:54-61)
GIVEN action IS AN Action
      kind IS A `o 1 r 2 kind of proceedings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(10) the proceedings are of a kind in sub-paragraphs (a) to (d)` MEANS
        action's `action commenced on` AT LEAST `o 1 r 1 the day these Rules come into operation`
    AND (   action's `action court level` EQUALS `Singapore International Commercial Court`
         OR kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(10)(b) proceedings in the General Division transferred out to the Singapore International Commercial Court`
         OR kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(10)(c) proceedings for the transfer of a case from the General Division to the Singapore International Commercial Court`
         OR kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(10)(d) an appeal or an originating application to the Court of Appeal relating to a decision of the Singapore International Commercial Court`)

@ref O 1 r 2(10) (src:54-61)
GIVEN action IS AN Action
      kind IS A `o 1 r 2 kind of proceedings`
      `the Court otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any other written law otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(10) these Rules apply to proceedings in or relating to the Singapore International Commercial Court` MEANS
    IF `o 1 r 2(10) the proceedings are of a kind in sub-paragraphs (a) to (d)` action kind
    THEN
        IF `the Court otherwise directs` OR `any other written law otherwise provides`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Unless the Court otherwise directs, and subject to any other written law"
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "these Rules do not apply to"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (10) speaks only of the four kinds of proceedings in sub-paragraphs (a) to (d)

