-- src:69 | Proceedings under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018
-- src:70 | Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018, section 448
-- src:71 | Order 25, Rule 6, Order 28 and Parts 3 and 4 of the Fourth Schedule read with Order 25
-- src:72 | 2.
-- src:73 | Proceedings relating to the winding up of limited liability partnerships
-- src:74 | Limited Liability Partnerships Act, section 57
-- src:75 | Order 25, Rule 6, Order 28, Parts 3 and 4 of the Fourth Schedule read with Order 25, and Order 50, Rule 3(2)
-- src:76 | 3.
-- src:77 | Proceedings relating to the winding up of variable capital companies and their sub‑funds or the receivership of the property of variable capital companies or sub‑funds
-- src:78 | Variable Capital Companies Act 2018, section 164
-- src:79 | Order 25, Rule 6, Order 28 and Parts 3 and 4 of the Fourth Schedule read with Order 25
-- src:80 | 4.
-- src:81 | Proceedings under Part IV of the Parliamentary Elections Act
-- src:82 | Parliamentary Elections Act, section 100
-- src:83 | Order 28 and Parts 3 and 4 of the Fourth Schedule read with Order 25
-- src:84 | [S 174/2026 wef 01/04/2026]
@ref O 1 r 2(11) the third column (src:62-84)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 1 r 2 kind of proceedings`
      `order number` IS A STRING
      `rule number` IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(11) the provision is in the third column for the kind of proceedings` MEANS
    -- "Order 28" and "Parts 3 and 4 of the Fourth Schedule read with Order 25" are cited whole: every rule of Order 28
    -- matches, whatever `rule number` is.  "Order 25, Rule 6" and "Order 50, Rule 3(2)" are cited to one rule.
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(11) item 1 proceedings under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
           THEN    (`order number` EQUALS "25" AND `rule number` EQUALS "6")
                OR (`order number` EQUALS "28")
                OR (`order number` EQUALS "Fourth Schedule Parts 3 and 4 read with Order 25")
        IF kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(11) item 2 proceedings relating to the winding up of limited liability partnerships`
           THEN    (`order number` EQUALS "25" AND `rule number` EQUALS "6")
                OR (`order number` EQUALS "28")
                OR (`order number` EQUALS "Fourth Schedule Parts 3 and 4 read with Order 25")
                OR (`order number` EQUALS "50" AND `rule number` EQUALS "3(2)")
        IF kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(11) item 3 proceedings relating to the winding up or receivership of variable capital companies or their sub-funds`
           THEN    (`order number` EQUALS "25" AND `rule number` EQUALS "6")
                OR (`order number` EQUALS "28")
                OR (`order number` EQUALS "Fourth Schedule Parts 3 and 4 read with Order 25")
        IF kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(11) item 4 proceedings under Part IV of the Parliamentary Elections Act`
           THEN    (`order number` EQUALS "28")
                OR (`order number` EQUALS "Fourth Schedule Parts 3 and 4 read with Order 25")
        OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref O 1 r 2(11) (src:62-84)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 1 r 2 kind of proceedings`
      `order number` IS A STRING
      `rule number` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(11) a provision of the Rules applies to proceedings of a kind in the Table` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2 other proceedings` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (11) speaks only of the four kinds of proceedings in its Table
        IF kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(3)(a) civil proceedings in the Supreme Court or the State Courts` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (11) speaks only of the four kinds of proceedings in its Table
        IF kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(8) proceedings under the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (11) speaks only of the four kinds of proceedings in its Table
        IF kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(10)(b) proceedings in the General Division transferred out to the Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (11) speaks only of the four kinds of proceedings in its Table
        IF kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(10)(c) proceedings for the transfer of a case from the General Division to the Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (11) speaks only of the four kinds of proceedings in its Table
        IF kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(10)(d) an appeal or an originating application to the Court of Appeal relating to a decision of the Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (11) speaks only of the four kinds of proceedings in its Table
        IF `o 1 r 2(11) the provision is in the third column for the kind of proceedings` kind `order number` `rule number` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "These Rules do not apply to proceedings of the kind specified in the first column of the following Table"

-- src:85 | (12) To avoid doubt, these Rules apply to any appeal arising from any proceedings mentioned in paragraphs (9) and (11).
@ref O 1 r 2(12) (src:85)
GIVEN `it is an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it arises from proceedings in the Family Division or of a kind in the Table in paragraph (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(12) these Rules apply to an appeal arising from proceedings mentioned in paragraphs (9) and (11)` MEANS
    IF `it is an appeal` AND `it arises from proceedings in the Family Division or of a kind in the Table in paragraph (11)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (12) speaks only of an appeal arising from those proceedings

-- src:86 | (13) The Second Schedule sets out the categories of cases to which specific provisions of these Rules do not apply, or apply with modifications.
@ref O 1 r 2(13) (src:86)
GIVEN `second schedule the case is in a category it sets out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2(13) specific provisions do not apply, or apply with modifications, to the case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `second schedule the case is in a category it sets out`
    WHEN JUST inCategory THEN
        IF inCategory
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (13) says nothing about a case outside the Second Schedule's categories
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Second Schedule is in another part's range, and in this text it is a heading with no table

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- the gathered answer: do these Rules apply to the proceedings?`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- E1, option B as guidance for gathering by hand only.  Paragraphs (8) to (11) take precedence over
-- paragraph (3) because paragraph (3) opens "Subject to this Rule"; paragraph (12) gives an appeal back
-- the Rules.  A JUST FALSE from any of (8) to (11) is the answer unless paragraph (12) applies.
-- Paragraph (11) gives no answer here: it is asked per provision.
-- src:13 | 2. —(1) Subject to the following provisions of this Rule, the Rules of Court (R 5) (called the revoked Rules of Court) are revoked. (2) The saving and transitional provisions set out in the First Schedule have effect.
@ref O 1 r 2 gathered (src:13)
GIVEN action IS AN Action
      kind IS A `o 1 r 2 kind of proceedings`
      `the decision is of a lower Court and was made in proceedings to which the revoked Rules of Court apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 or its subsidiary legislation provides otherwise` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Court otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any other written law otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an appeal arising from proceedings in the Family Division or of a kind in the Table in paragraph (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 2 these Rules apply to the proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `o 1 r 2(12) these Rules apply to an appeal arising from proceedings mentioned in paragraphs (9) and (11)` TRUE `it is an appeal arising from proceedings in the Family Division or of a kind in the Table in paragraph (11)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 1 r 2(8) these Rules apply to proceedings under the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` kind `the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 or its subsidiary legislation provides otherwise` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "These Rules do not apply to proceedings under the Criminal Procedure Code 2010"
        IF `o 1 r 2(9) these Rules apply to proceedings in the Family Division of the High Court` action EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "These Rules do not apply to proceedings in the Family Division of the High Court"
        IF `o 1 r 2(10) these Rules apply to proceedings in or relating to the Singapore International Commercial Court` action kind `the Court otherwise directs` `any other written law otherwise provides` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "these Rules do not apply to"
        IF `o 1 r 2(10) the proceedings are of a kind in sub-paragraphs (a) to (d)` action kind AND (`the Court otherwise directs` OR `any other written law otherwise provides`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Unless the Court otherwise directs, and subject to any other written law"
        IF kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(11) item 1 proceedings under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` OR kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(11) item 2 proceedings relating to the winding up of limited liability partnerships` OR kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(11) item 3 proceedings relating to the winding up or receivership of variable capital companies or their sub-funds` OR kind EQUALS `o 1 r 2(11) item 4 proceedings under Part IV of the Parliamentary Elections Act` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (11) disapplies the Rules except for the provisions in its Table, so ask `o 1 r 2(11)` provision by provision
        IF `o 1 r 2(3)(a) these Rules apply to civil proceedings commenced on or after 1 April 2022` action kind EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 1 r 2(3)(b) these Rules apply with modifications to an appeal or originating application to an appellate court` action `the decision is of a lower Court and was made in proceedings to which the revoked Rules of Court apply` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): none of paragraphs (3) and (8) to (12) answers for these proceedings

