§ `Order 1, Rule 3 -- general definitions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3(1), opening words`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:88 | 3. —(1) In these Rules, unless the context otherwise requires — “action” means proceedings commenced by an originating claim or an originating application;
@ref O 1 r 3(1) opening words, “unless the context otherwise requires” (src:88)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 3(1) a defined term has its defined meaning` MEANS
    IF `the context otherwise requires`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the context otherwise requires"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3(1) -- the terms from "action" to "defendant"`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:88 | 3. —(1) In these Rules, unless the context otherwise requires — “action” means proceedings commenced by an originating claim or an originating application;
@ref O 1 r 3(1) “action” (src:88)
GIVEN document IS A `Document kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 3(1) proceedings commenced by a document are an action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF document EQUALS `Originating claim` OR document EQUALS `Originating application` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“action” means proceedings commenced by an originating claim or an originating application"

-- src:89 | “appellate Court” means the Court to which an appeal is brought or is being brought;
@ref O 1 r 3(1) “appellate Court” (src:89)
GIVEN `the court is the one to which an appeal is brought or is being brought` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 3(1) a court is the appellate Court` MEANS
    IF `the court is the one to which an appeal is brought or is being brought`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“appellate Court” means the Court to which an appeal is brought or is being brought"

-- src:90 | “Appellate Division” means the Appellate Division of the High Court;
@ref O 1 r 3(1) “Appellate Division” (src:90)
GIVEN level IS A `Court level`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 3(1) a court is the Appellate Division` MEANS
    IF level EQUALS `Appellate Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Appellate Division” means the Appellate Division of the High Court"

-- src:91 | “attend” includes the appearance by any person using electronic, mechanical or any other means permitted by the Court;
@ref O 1 r 3(1) “attend” (src:91)
GIVEN `the person appears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appears by electronic, mechanical or other means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court permitted those means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 3(1) a person attends` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person appears` AND `the person appears by electronic, mechanical or other means` AND `the Court permitted those means` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“attend” includes the appearance by any person using electronic, mechanical or any other means permitted by the Court"

-- src:92 | “bailiff” includes the Registrar, any clerk or other officer of the Court charged with the duties of a bailiff;
@ref O 1 r 3(1) “bailiff” (src:92)
GIVEN `the person is the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a clerk or other officer of the Court charged with the duties of a bailiff` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 3(1) a person is a bailiff` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is the Registrar` OR `the person is a clerk or other officer of the Court charged with the duties of a bailiff` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“bailiff” includes the Registrar, any clerk or other officer of the Court charged with the duties of a bailiff"

-- src:93 | “case conference” means a case conference as described in Order 9, Rule 1;
@ref O 1 r 3(1) “case conference” (src:93)
GIVEN `o 9 r 1 the meeting is a case conference as described` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 3(1) a meeting is a case conference` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 9 r 1 the meeting is a case conference as described`
    WHEN JUST described THEN
        IF described
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“case conference” means a case conference as described in Order 9, Rule 1"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Order 9, Rule 1 is in another part's range

-- src:94 | “Civil Procedure Convention” means any of the conventions set out in the Third Schedule and includes any convention, treaty or agreement of any description or any provision of such convention, treaty or agreement between different States relating to civil procedure in the Court;
@ref O 1 r 3(1) “Civil Procedure Convention” (src:94)
GIVEN `third schedule the convention is set out in the Third Schedule` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is a convention, treaty or agreement between different States relating to civil procedure in the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 3(1) an instrument is a Civil Procedure Convention` MEANS
    CONSIDER `third schedule the convention is set out in the Third Schedule`
    WHEN JUST inSchedule THEN
        IF inSchedule OR `the instrument is a convention, treaty or agreement between different States relating to civil procedure in the Court`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes any convention, treaty or agreement of any description or any provision of such convention, treaty or agreement between different States relating to civil procedure in the Court"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the instrument is a convention, treaty or agreement between different States relating to civil procedure in the Court`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Third Schedule is in another part's range

-- src:95 | “claimant” includes a party in the position of a claimant in a counterclaim;
