`o 1 r 3(1) a statement is a counterclaim` MEANS
    `o 1 r 3(1) a statement is a statement of claim` `the statement sets out the material facts which constitute the cause of action`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3(1) -- "Court": four limbs, gathered by hand`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- E1, option B as guidance for gathering by hand only: the four limbs of "Court" each get their own
-- function (option C), and the one function after them gathers the routes so that a reader can ask
-- the question once.  No construct gathers by name.

-- src:97 | “Court” means — ( a )
-- src:98 | the General Division or a judge sitting in the General Division, whether sitting in open court or in chambers;
@ref O 1 r 3(1) “Court”, limb (a) (src:97-98)
GIVEN sitting IS A Sitting
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 3(1) limb (a) the General Division or a judge sitting in it` MEANS
        sitting's `sitting court level` EQUALS `General Division`
    AND (   sitting's `sitting decision maker` EQUALS `The court itself`
         OR sitting's `sitting decision maker` EQUALS `A Judge`)

-- src:99 | ( b )
-- src:100 | a District Court or a District Judge, whether sitting in open court or in chambers;
@ref O 1 r 3(1) “Court”, limb (b) (src:99-100)
GIVEN sitting IS A Sitting
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 3(1) limb (b) a District Court or a District Judge` MEANS
        (   sitting's `sitting court level` EQUALS `District Court`
        AND sitting's `sitting decision maker` EQUALS `The court itself`)
    OR  sitting's `sitting decision maker` EQUALS `A District Judge`

-- src:101 | ( c )
-- src:102 | the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal, or a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal where appropriate; or
@ref O 1 r 3(1) “Court”, limb (c) (src:101-102)
GIVEN sitting IS A Sitting
      `it is appropriate for a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal to act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 3(1) limb (c) the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal, or a judge sitting in either` MEANS
        (   sitting's `sitting court level` EQUALS `Appellate Division`
         OR sitting's `sitting court level` EQUALS `Court of Appeal`)
    AND (   sitting's `sitting decision maker` EQUALS `The court itself`
         OR (    sitting's `sitting decision maker` EQUALS `A Judge`
             AND `it is appropriate for a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal to act`))

-- src:103 | ( d )
-- src:104 | in cases where he or she is empowered to act, a Magistrate or the Registrar;
@ref O 1 r 3(1) “Court”, limb (d) (src:103-104)
GIVEN sitting IS A Sitting
      `the Magistrate or the Registrar is empowered to act in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 3(1) limb (d) in cases where empowered, a Magistrate or the Registrar` MEANS
        (   sitting's `sitting decision maker` EQUALS `A Magistrate`
         OR sitting's `sitting decision maker` EQUALS `The Registrar`)
    AND `the Magistrate or the Registrar is empowered to act in the case`

-- src:97 | “Court” means — ( a )
-- src:98 | the General Division or a judge sitting in the General Division, whether sitting in open court or in chambers;
-- src:99 | ( b )
-- src:100 | a District Court or a District Judge, whether sitting in open court or in chambers;
-- src:101 | ( c )
-- src:102 | the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal, or a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal where appropriate; or
-- src:103 | ( d )
-- src:104 | in cases where he or she is empowered to act, a Magistrate or the Registrar;
@ref O 1 r 3(1) “Court” (src:97-104)
GIVEN sitting IS A Sitting
      `it is appropriate for a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Magistrate or the Registrar is empowered to act in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 1 r 3(1) a decision-maker sitting in a court is the Court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `o 1 r 3(1) limb (a) the General Division or a judge sitting in it` sitting THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 1 r 3(1) limb (b) a District Court or a District Judge` sitting THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 1 r 3(1) limb (c) the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal, or a judge sitting in either` sitting `it is appropriate for a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal to act` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `o 1 r 3(1) limb (d) in cases where empowered, a Magistrate or the Registrar` sitting `the Magistrate or the Registrar is empowered to act in the case` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (    (   sitting's `sitting court level` EQUALS `Appellate Division`
                 OR sitting's `sitting court level` EQUALS `Court of Appeal`)
            AND sitting's `sitting decision maker` EQUALS `A Judge`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal where appropriate"
        IF (   sitting's `sitting decision maker` EQUALS `A Magistrate`
            OR sitting's `sitting decision maker` EQUALS `The Registrar`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in cases where he or she is empowered to act, a Magistrate or the Registrar"
        IF sitting's `sitting court level` EQUALS `Magistrate's Court` AND sitting's `sitting decision maker` EQUALS `The court itself` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the definition names "a Magistrate" but not the Magistrate's Court as a body
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Court” means"


-- src:105 | “court fees” has the meaning given by Order 25, Rule 1;
@ref O 1 r 3(1) “court fees” (src:105)
